  "id": "Compound::DB00936 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Salicylic Acid is implicated in the transport of organic anions through the regulation of Slc22a6, as evidenced by its binding to Slc22a7 and Slc22a8, which are involved in organic anion transport. This suggests that Salicylic Acid may modulate the activity of these transporters, potentially influencing the cellular uptake of anions. The connection between Salicylic Acid and Slc22a6 is further supported by the fact that Piroxicam, a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) that shares a common ancestor with Salicylic Acid, binds to Slc22a6. This indicates a possible pathway where Salicylic Acid, through its interaction with NSAIDs, may affect Slc22a6 function. The integration of these relationships highlights a potential mechanism by which Salicylic Acid influences the transport of organic anions, possibly through the regulation of Slc22a6, which is a key player in anion transport across cell membranes. The evidence suggests a direct or indirect interaction between Salicylic Acid and Slc22a6, mediated through the involvement of other transporters and compounds.",
